{# -------------------------------------------------------------------
   Formulation extractor – multi-experiment
   Variables injected by Python:
     PAPER_TEXT    – full paper text (markdown)
     EXPERIMENTS   – JSON list of experiment objects [{"id": "EXPT-001", ...}, …]
     SCHEMA        – FormulationPass JSON Schema
   ------------------------------------------------------------------- #}

Extract cryobiology formulation data for ALL experiments listed in EXPERIMENTS from PAPER_TEXT.
Return ONLY JSON conforming to FormulationPass schema.

CRITICAL RULES:
1. Extract only information explicitly stated in PAPER_TEXT.
2. Never hallucinate or infer missing data.
3. Each formulation MUST include the correct "experiment_id" matching one of the EXPERIMENTS ids.
4. Each formulation must have unique content.
5. Return only valid JSON.

EXTRACTION PROTOCOL:
• Consider every formulation described anywhere in PAPER_TEXT.
• Map each formulation to the corresponding experiment by context. If uncertain, omit the formulation.
• Follow the same component extraction rules used in the single-experiment prompt.

MANDATORY FIELDS per formulation:
- experiment_id: One of {{ EXPERIMENTS | map(attribute='id') | list }}
- label
- components (>=1) – see COMPONENT RULES below
- quote – must capture ALL numeric values for all components

COMPONENT RULES (identical to single-experiment version):
- Extract each component separately; never combine components.
- Do NOT include quantities in the component label.
- Required component fields:
  • role: "CPA", "ADJUVANT", or "CARRIER"
  • agent_id: InChIKey or null per rules
  • amount: {"value_type": "point"|"range", ...}
  • unit: required
  • quote: exact text fragment containing the component's quantity

OPTIONAL FIELDS:
Include dependent_properties only if PAPER_TEXT reports explicit numerical measurement.

OUTPUT:
Return only the JSON object.

SCHEMA:
{{ SCHEMA }}

PAPER_TEXT:
{{ PAPER_TEXT }}
